  "solution": {
    "text": "Moment of inertia of circular ring about an axis passing through its centre of mass and perpendicular to its plane<br /><br /><math><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />Here, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math><br /><br /><math><msup><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br /><br />or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math><br /><br />Therefore, diameter of ring = 4 m."
